WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:05.890
The latest big screen Jumanji chapter has
some very good moments and just as many disappointing

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:06.890
ones.

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:11.089
Here are three of the most exciting things
about Jumanji: The Next Level, and three things

00:00:11.089 --> 00:00:12.730
filmmakers could've skipped.

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:13.809
Best: Kevin Hart

00:00:13.809 --> 00:00:17.430
Kevin Hart is obviously a funny guy the man's
a professional stand-up comedian and he's

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:20.800
made a lucrative second career for himself
as a movie star.

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:25.290
Hart usually plays the same kind of characters,
and they tend to act and sound exactly like

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:26.930
Hart does on stage.

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:31.470
In Jumanji: The Next Level, Hart's screen
persona is wildly different, because it has

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:32.470
to be.

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:37.260
Since the avatar he plays, weapons keeper
and zoologist Franklin "Mouse" Finbar, spends

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:42.879
a lot of the film inhabited by easy-going,
talkative, retired restaurant manager Milo,

00:00:42.879 --> 00:00:46.940
played by Danny Glover, he has to act like
Milo by way of Mouse.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:52.039
It's a tricky balancing act, and Hart succeeds,
elevating his performance beyond just an impression

00:00:52.039 --> 00:00:53.949
of the soft-spoken Glover.

00:00:53.949 --> 00:00:58.250
That would grow tiring after 45 minutes of
screen time, so Hart doesn't try to do the

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:03.710
voice exactly, but rather nail the vibe of
an old man getting a huge kick out of traipsing

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:08.420
around a video game and suddenly knowing dozens
of animal fun facts which he'll spout off

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:09.420
at random.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:13.930
Hart brings the comic relief, as is his way,
but he also brings a sweetness and softness

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:16.740
that's otherwise lacking in a movie full of
action.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:17.890
Worst: Johnson's DeVito impression

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:23.369
Dwayne Johnson can do it all: action, comedy,
animated musicals … So, what can't "The

00:01:23.369 --> 00:01:24.369
Rock" do?

00:01:24.369 --> 00:01:25.750
He can't do Danny DeVito.

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:30.369
The plot of Jumanji: The Next Level calls
for Johnson to perform an extended imitation

00:01:30.369 --> 00:01:33.780
of the distinctively voiced star of It's Always
Sunny in Philadelphia.

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:40.909
"If you're dealt a bunch of lemons, you gotta
take those lemons and stuff them down somebody's

00:01:40.909 --> 00:01:41.909
throat!"

00:01:41.909 --> 00:01:46.189
While Johnson tries admirably, he just can't
pull it off, and the results are awkward.

00:01:46.189 --> 00:01:50.670
Sometimes he just speaks loudly to evoke the
spirit of DeVito, ignoring the New Jersey

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:52.039
accent entirely.

00:01:52.039 --> 00:01:55.000
Sometimes, Johnson forgets to do any sort
of accent at all.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:59.750
While his comic timing is on point, Johnson's
swing-and-a-miss at the proper voice is hard

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:00.960
to ignore.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:07.350
"I just passed my driver's test last month,
again."

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:08.560
Best: Karen Gillan

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:14.110
Since leaving behind her breakout role as
Amelia Pond on Doctor Who in 2012, Karen Gillan

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:16.420
has certainly worked steadily.

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:21.170
She's a supporting player in the vast Marvel
Cinematic Universe, almost unrecognizable

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:23.480
as blue-skinned alien Nebula.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:28.069
She also starred, however briefly, in her
own ABC sitcom, Selfie.

00:02:28.069 --> 00:02:32.730
Portraying video game heroine Ruby Roundhouse
in Jumanji: Welcome to the Jungle increased

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:37.150
her profile, and while that was a big movie,
it still amounted to a supporting role.

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:41.650
But Gillan, and Ruby, take center stage in
Jumanji: The Next Level.

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:46.060
She's arguably the most prominent member of
the all-star cast, leading the expedition

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:50.090
through the game world and enjoying a couple
of showcase action sequences.

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:54.680
Gillan also provides the emotional center
of the movie with the personality of Martha

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:59.580
inside, she tells boyfriend Spencer that he's
going to be okay, and that their relationship

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:03.489
will be okay, too... all while scaling a mountain
made of ice.

00:03:03.489 --> 00:03:07.769
Gillan completely steals the movie, making
good on the promise she showed a decade ago

00:03:07.769 --> 00:03:08.769
on Doctor Who.

00:03:08.769 --> 00:03:09.769
Worst: A leering camera

00:03:09.769 --> 00:03:14.620
Karen Gillan triumphs with a positive, winning
performance despite the way the script and

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:17.349
filmmakers treat the Ruby Roundhouse character.

00:03:17.349 --> 00:03:21.920
It's understood that her character is supposed
to be an example of unnecessarily provocative

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:23.799
female video game characters.

00:03:23.799 --> 00:03:29.079
Ruby engages yet again in a lot of stunts
and combat dressed in a crop top and short-shorts,

00:03:29.079 --> 00:03:30.239
putting Gillan on display.

00:03:30.239 --> 00:03:32.890
"Why am I wearing this outfit in a jungle?

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:37.489
Tiny little shorts and a leather halter top.

00:03:37.489 --> 00:03:38.620
What is this?"

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:42.500
Showing off a little skin is something to
be expected from major movies, but it seems

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:47.329
inappropriate for Jumanji: The Next Level,
a family film in which the young female characters

00:03:47.329 --> 00:03:51.360
are just as viable as warriors and adventurers
as the male characters.

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:54.319
Making things seem extra sleazy is how Gillan
is filmed.

00:03:54.319 --> 00:03:59.469
There are plenty of shots of her bare midriff
and rear end, with next to no comparable exploitative

00:03:59.469 --> 00:04:02.140
photography of musclebound co-star Dwayne
Johnson.

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:03.409
Best: Rhys Darby

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:08.120
There's a whole different level of Jumanji:
The Next Level: a gentle satirization of video

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:09.849
game conventions and cliches.

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:13.950
The film is structured like a video game,
arranged into different worlds and areas,

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:19.640
including a desert, the jungle, mountains,
and naturally, at the end, a remote and punishing

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:20.640
castle.

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:24.210
The funniest video game send-up in the film,
the one thing that makes viewers realize how

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:30.000
ridiculous and unrealistic video games can
be, is the return of Nigel Billingsley, an

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:34.750
NPC, or "non-player character" that serves
as a guide to the characters.

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:40.220
Comic actor Rhys Darby is once again all in
on his portrayal of the soulless, smiling,

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:44.990
helpful Nigel as he moves the action along,
urging characters to read instruction-giving

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:49.090
letters out loud and congratulating the heroes
on a job well done.

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:53.590
And when he's in the scene but doesn't have
a line, Darby quietly and perfectly stands

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:57.639
on the periphery doing and saying absolutely
nothing, just like a real NPC.

00:04:57.639 --> 00:04:59.190
Worst: So much wasted talent

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:02.910
Jumanji: The Next Level debuted in theaters
in December 2019.

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:07.510
The end of the year is second only to summer
in terms of the big movie studios rolling

00:05:07.510 --> 00:05:12.240
out their biggest, flashiest blockbusters,
and to get noticed in a crowded marketplace,

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:16.440
Jumanji filmmakers stacked their cast with
a number of major movie stars.

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:21.330
The main cast consists of heavy hitters like
Dwayne Johnson, Jack Black, and Kevin Hart,

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:25.850
and their adventure through video game deserts
and castles takes up the bulk of the film's

00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:26.850
runtime.

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:31.630
Other well-known, well-liked, and bankable
actors round out the Jumanji: The Next Level

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:34.000
cast, but there just isn't enough for them
to do.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:38.020
It's disappointing that the producers hired
such notable people if they were barely going

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:39.020
to use them.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:43.919
The great Danny DeVito and Danny Glover appear
early in the film as Spencer's grumpy grandfather

00:05:43.919 --> 00:05:46.500
Eddie and estranged friend Milo, respectively.

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:51.630
Then, when their souls take up residence in
the bodies of video game avatars, they disappear

00:05:51.630 --> 00:05:55.880
in favor of the avatar actors doing impressions
of DeVito and Glover.

00:05:55.880 --> 00:06:00.259
Nick Jonas and Colin Hanks reprise their roles
from Jumanji: Welcome to the Jungle, but only

00:06:00.259 --> 00:06:02.740
show up when the film is nearly over.

00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:08.770
Additionally, recognizable and reliable sitcom
stars John Ross Bowie and Lamorne Morris appear

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:13.289
inexplicably in tiny parts, delivering just
a few lines each.

